VeridianOS: state internal invariants GCC cannot see (-Wnull-dereference)

GCC reported -Wnull-dereference ("potential null pointer dereference") at
the remaining places in GLib, libgobject and libgirepository (target and
host-tools builds alike). In each case a helper can return NULL in
general, but not for the arguments used there; the build keeps
g_assert() enabled, and g_assertion_message_expr() is noreturn, so a
g_assert() stating the invariant is the explicit check the compiler sees.
Valid input takes the same paths as before; an invariant violation now
fails a named assertion instead of crashing on NULL.

- glib/gkeyfile.c (g_key_file_set_group_comment,
  g_key_file_get_group_comment): the named group was already found, and
  every named group is followed in key_file->groups by at least the
  unnamed top-comment group (always the last node), so its node and the
  node after it (which holds the comment) exist.
- glib/gvariant-parser.c (string_parse, bytestring_parse): only called
  after the next token was peeked to be a (byte)string, so
  token_stream_get() returns a token.
- gobject/gsignal.c: handler_list_ensure() looks up the key it has just
  inserted; handlers_find() and the three signal_parse_name() callers look
  up registered signal ids (signal nodes are never removed); the first
  element of a class_closure_bsa exists because the array is only created
  together with it.
- gobject/gtype.c (type_node_fundamental_info_I): a type's fundamental
  type is registered before it, and none of the four callers handles a
  NULL result; the NULL return is replaced by the assertion.
- gobject/gtypemodule.c (complete_type_info, complete_interface_info):
  GType only asks the plugin a type or interface was registered with.
- girepository/girparser.c (parse_type_internal): str is the caller's
  string or a temporary built with g_strdup()/g_strdup_printf(); GCC
  cannot see that those return non-NULL and followed a NULL str through
  the NULL branch of the g_str_has_prefix() macro to "*str" (line 684).
  The assertion sits before the prefix checks; the existing scan-build
  assertion further down is left alone.
- girepository/girwriter.c (gi_ir_writer_write, reported inside the
  G_TYPE_FROM_INSTANCE() macro at gobject/gtype.h:646): the info at an
  index below gi_repository_get_n_infos() exists, so it is asserted
  before the type dispatch whose fallback g_error() dereferenced it.

